KZ3 patch 1068 (SPU pass 52, diagnostic, no behaviour change): the [pm-end] post-mortem (a SPURS policy-module lane run
that ended anywhere but exitToKernel, which strands the job it had claimed) now keeps 256 drain steps (was 32) and
marks the control-flow events that bypass the trampoline ring: interrupt taken (I:srr0), iret register restore
(R:pc), restart dispatch longjmp (X:pc), drain resume at a lifted entry (D:pc), the driver's restart entry (E:pc), each
with the host depth; the line also gives the wid, image, resident overlay, interrupt enable, event status/mask, srr0,
the saved-register state (irq_saved, resume pc) and steps, written as one buffer. Found need: KZ3's quit hang, the
Amadeus mixer job (job_0127a180, wid 5) ends its lane at pc 0x4D70 inside the job with status RUNNING, depth 0, and
the 32-step ring could not say how.
